

Yep, yep, yep, here it is at last



                          PreventDelete
                          
                          A tool against modem hackers !
                          
Written 20-08-1992 by The Lazy Coder of CHRYSEIS
                   for Black Krypt BBS (+32 81 226726)
                   
                   
What does it do ?
-----------------

     Patch the trackdisk device in order to prevent (if necessery) any FORMAT
     command.
     
     Patch the scsi device, the suprascsi device and the gvpscsi device
     the same way (send us other drivers name to complete the list).
     
     Patch the dos library in order to prevent any DeleteFile command.
     
Limits
------

     The shell command 'Delete' still works ! (it doesn't use the shared
     dos library -mmm bad programmed commodore guys :-)
     
     This program has been coded on a kick 1.2 amiga 500, without hard
     drive. Does it work really for scsi device ? Wait and see ...

     Startup routine not included yet : you'll have to type
     'run <nil: >nil: PreventDelete'. It's 8 AM and I'm too tired
     to add this little thing... next release !
     
How does it work
----------------

     When the window is active, you have two options : BBS mode and
     standalone.
     
     BBS mode is for modem owners only : it makes the protection active
     only when the CD (carrier detect) is on (i.e. when someone is
     calling you or when you are calling someone).
     
     standalone is mostly for BBS users who keep their computer running
     24 hours a day : if activated, this option makes the program deny
     any Destructive attempt and logs these attempts in the file
     'ram:PreventDelete.log'.
     
